// The finale: two springs on either side of a river with two fords.
name Headwaters
rule B1/S012345678
steps 5
hint Two springs, one river, two fords. Trace each flood back to where it started.
tip Each spring is the first ripple grown for five generations. Find both centres; the river only clips the edges.
intro A river of stone with two fords. On each side, a spring that flooded for five generations.
outro Rivers clip what they cannot stop. The springs still tell where they rose.
